# Line endings, decided here so they are not decided by whoever cloned.
#
# Git's Windows default is `core.autocrlf=true`, which rewrites LF to CRLF on
# checkout. GitHub's windows-latest runners use it. That is fine for source —
# and fatal for a file whose exact bytes are the assertion.
#
# `packages/dvm/test/commands/color_off_golden.txt` records, byte for byte,
# what dvm printed before colour existed; `color_test.dart` compares the
# program's output against it and the whole point is that not one byte moved.
# Checked out with CRLF, the golden could never match output built from `\n`,
# so the Windows job went red on a difference git had introduced. `-text`
# turns EOL conversion off in both directions: the bytes on disk are the bytes
# committed, on every platform. It does NOT disable diffs — that is the `diff`
# attribute — so the golden stays reviewable when it legitimately changes.
*_golden.txt -text

# Shell scripts are read by a POSIX shell, which does not want CR. Pinned to
# LF so a checkout on Windows cannot produce a script that a WSL or git-bash
# run then chokes on. `text eol=lf` rather than `-text`: these are ordinary
# text and should stay diffable and mergeable as text.
*.sh text eol=lf
